snippet.textDisplay:
@zci-o9i Gorbachev and Deng Xiaoping allowed capitalism because of the abject failure of socialist economic policy; that didn’t undo the millions murdered in the bloody revolutions required to bring about the socialist state, it ignores the fact that both of those countries for decades outlawed private property, it ignores the totalitarian states that mercilessly crushed dissent. 

As for why capitalists shouldn’t tolerate Marxists, it’s because it’s a subversive ideology with the express intent of revolution and destroying it all for some utopian vision of the future that will never come to pass. 

And to reiterate, socialist economic policy is abjectly horrifyingly incompetent. It completely ignores incentive structures, and just tries to wish things into existence. Rent control, universal healthcare, “affordable” housing, they all distort the market and turn a bad situation into something worse, because you think the government can know more and manage more effectively than 300 million people making small individual decisions for themselves.

